Body:
I believe this issue is a duplicate after reading the linked threads above, however, there may be more to this.

I ran into a similar type of indefinite hanging in the CLI due to watcher. Subdirectories were fine. I'm not sure whether the fix in #25842 is going to fix that too, since I'm not sure whether the bundling for CLI differs.

I was able to work around it by disabling watcher on a big Library subdirectory, in  in a new `openconfig.json` file at my repo root. According to Claude, watcher was falling back to polling, which explains the delay. I got answers instantaneously after adding this.

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "snapshot": false,
  "watcher": {
    "ignore": ["Library/**"]
  }
}
```

Workaround that injects a provider config from the `config` hook:
```typescript
const plugin: Plugin = async () => ({
  // The config() hook fires before opencode reads cfg.provider, so it
  // can both default missing fields and inject the model dict that
  // opencode 1.14.31+ requires for non-models.dev providers. The
  // provider.models() hook is silently skipped for providers that
  // aren't in the models.dev catalog (provider.ts:1153 in opencode),
  // so injecting models here is the only path that registers them.
  config: async (input) => {
    const providers = (input.provider ??= {})
    const cfg = (providers.magos ??= {})
    const base = baseURL(cfg)
    cfg.name ??= "Magos"
    cfg.npm ??= "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"
    // Default options.baseURL so a bare opencode.json works. The /v1 is
    // what the SDK appends paths to (POST /v1/chat/completions).
    const options = (cfg.options ??= {})
    options.baseURL ??= `${base}/v1`

    const registry = await fetchRegistry(base)
    if (!registry) return

    const models = (cfg.models ??= {})
    for (const entry of registry.entries) {
      if (entry.deprecated_at) continue
      const id = namespacedId(entry)
      models[id] ??= entryToModel(entry)
    }
  },
})
```

