I read the limitations you describe, several points were indeed raised by others and there are some such changes implemented in shuvcode to make subagents states more explorable in the TUI. 

Unfortunately i don't expect opencode's team to settle on any specific implementation of agents teams given how orchestration is a hot topic right now and it's chrnging very fast, so I guess the more likely route is to just open a PR with exactly what you [wrote](https://github.com/panwar-stack/opencode-agent-team#gaps-remaining--plugin-api-limitations) about the limitations of the current opencode plugins sdk to ask the team to extend it to expose the parts that would be needed for advanced multiagents orchestration systems such as yours. This does not require them to develop or commit to maintaining a whole new orchestration system this way, they just have to provide interfaces to what is already in the codebase, and this will certainly be useful to a lot of future advanced plugins. 

If you open such a pr please link here, i will upvote ! And I advise anyone reading this thread and interested in agents teams and the future orchestration systems beyond to massively upvote too !
